    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "txt_0284",
      "reading_order": 293,
      "section": "HEATER (GLOW PLUG) RELAY CHECK (K13)",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 57.939800000000005,
        "t": 713.4786068359374,
        "r": 280.9070000000001,
        "b": 688.9397469606776
      },
      "content": "HEATER (GLOW PLUG) RELAY CHECK (K13)",
      "level": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0285",
      "reading_order": 294,
      "section": "HEATER (GLOW PLUG) RELAY CHECK (K13)",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 55.8425,
        "t": 675.2303068359375,
        "r": 291.4493000000002,
        "b": 640.0301492035388
      },
      "content": "Connect the relay coil voltage across the relay coil terminals.  The relay should activate if coil is okay."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0286",
      "reading_order": 295,
      "section": "HEATER (GLOW PLUG) RELAY CHECK (K13)",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 55.842500000000015,
        "t": 624.6611068359376,
        "r": 291.38770000000034,
        "b": 602.1032492035389
      },
      "content": "Connect a voltage source to one side of relay contacts."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0287",
      "reading_order": 296,
      "section": "HEATER (GLOW PLUG) RELAY CHECK (K13)",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 55.842500000000015,
        "t": 586.7342068359377,
        "r": 291.5989000000003,
        "b": 526.249449203539
      },
      "content": "Connect a voltmeter to other side of relay contact  and  voltage  source.    If  voltage  appears when relay energizes, the contact is good.  The voltage reading appears in reverse order when checking normally closed (NC) contacts."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "txt_0288",
      "reading_order": 297,
      "section": "[F]",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 161.8016,
        "t": 510.91520683593745,
        "r": 177.12560000000002,
        "b": 500.09594696067757
      },
      "content": "[F]",
      "level": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "txt_0289",
      "reading_order": 298,
      "section": "FUEL SOLENOID CHECK (K14)",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 80.95760000000001,
        "t": 486.36680683593744,
        "r": 257.95279999999997,
        "b": 475.54754696067755
      },
      "content": "FUEL SOLENOID CHECK (K14)",
      "level": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0290",
      "reading_order": 299,
      "section": "FUEL SOLENOID CHECK (K14)",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 47.5654,
        "t": 461.8381068359375,
        "r": 291.72029999999995,
        "b": 439.2230492035387
      },
      "content": "If there is fuel to the injection pump, but no fuel at the injection nozzle, the fuel solenoid may be defective."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0291",
      "reading_order": 300,
      "section": "FUEL SOLENOID CHECK (K14)",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 47.56650000000001,
        "t": 423.9101068359375,
        "r": 291.56630000000047,
        "b": 363.4253492035388
      },
      "content": "To check solenoid operation, watch for solenoid actuation when B+ is applied (start switch in start or run position).  If there is no actuation when B+ is applied, the fuel solenoid must be replaced.  When B+ is removed, the solenoid must de-activate."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "txt_0292",
      "reading_order": 301,
      "section": "[G]",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 160.7811,
        "t": 348.0365068359375,
        "r": 178.10910000000004,
        "b": 337.2172469606776
      },
      "content": "[G]",
      "level": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "txt_0293",
      "reading_order": 302,
      "section": "START/STOP SWITCH CHECK (S11)",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 67.5207,
        "t": 323.48810683593746,
        "r": 271.38869999999986,
        "b": 312.66884696067757
      },
      "content": "START/STOP SWITCH CHECK (S11)",
      "level": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0294",
      "reading_order": 303,
      "section": "START/STOP SWITCH CHECK (S11)",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 55.8425,
        "t": 298.9594068359375,
        "r": 196.10569999999993,
        "b": 289.04384920353874
      },
      "content": "Remove battery B+ cable."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0295",
      "reading_order": 304,
      "section": "START/STOP SWITCH CHECK (S11)",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 55.8425,
        "t": 273.7309068359375,
        "r": 250.84720000000007,
        "b": 263.81534920353874
      },
      "content": "Place ohmmeter leads across switch."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0296",
      "reading_order": 305,
      "section": "START/STOP SWITCH CHECK (S11)",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 329.2156,
        "t": 737.9892068359376,
        "r": 564.9499999999991,
        "b": 664.8621492035389
      },
      "content": "Open  and  close  switch  while  observing  the ohmmeter.    A  normally  open  (NO)  switch should indicate infinite resistance when open and continuity when closed.   A normally closed (NC)  switch  should  indicate  continuity  when closed and infinite resistance when open."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0297",
      "reading_order": 306,
      "section": "START/STOP SWITCH CHECK (S11)",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 329.2156,
        "t": 652.0440068359377,
        "r": 475.23949999999985,
        "b": 642.1284492035389
      },
      "content": "Replace switch if defective."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "txt_0298",
      "reading_order": 307,
      "section": "[H]",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 434.4945,
        "t": 629.2900068359374,
        "r": 451.15049999999997,
        "b": 618.4707469606776
      },
      "content": "[H]",
      "level": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "txt_0299",
      "reading_order": 308,
      "section": "POWER RELAY CHECK (A11-K12)",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 346.2237,
        "t": 606.9532068359374,
        "r": 539.2761000000005,
        "b": 596.1339469606776
      },
      "content": "POWER RELAY CHECK (A11-K12)",
      "level": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0300",
      "reading_order": 309,
      "section": "POWER RELAY CHECK (A11-K12)",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 320.9386,
        "t": 584.5783068359375,
        "r": 564.8163000000002,
        "b": 562.0204492035388
      },
      "content": "Make certain that the generator set starting battery is good before beginning this check."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0301",
      "reading_order": 310,
      "section": "POWER RELAY CHECK (A11-K12)",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 329.2161,
        "t": 549.2023068359375,
        "r": 565.0835999999999,
        "b": 514.0021492035388
      },
      "content": "Unplug CB12-2A from the circuit breaker.  Note the markings on the wire to select the correct one."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0302",
      "reading_order": 311,
      "section": "POWER RELAY CHECK (A11-K12)",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 329.2150000000001,
        "t": 501.18400683593757,
        "r": 564.9835000000003,
        "b": 465.98384920353885
      },
      "content": "Locate S6 (oil pressure switch) on the generator set (see Figure 2-2).  Find the grounded side of S6, using a continuity tester."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0303",
      "reading_order": 312,
      "section": "POWER RELAY CHECK (A11-K12)",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 329.2139000000001,
        "t": 453.1657068359376,
        "r": 564.8790000000002,
        "b": 430.6078492035389
      },
      "content": "Use a jumper to ground the non-grounded side of S6."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0304",
      "reading_order": 313,
      "section": "POWER RELAY CHECK (A11-K12)",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 329.2128000000001,
        "t": 417.78970683593764,
        "r": 564.7810999999999,
        "b": 369.94724920353895
      },
      "content": "Use a second jumper from the B+ terminal on the  control  board to apply B+ to the SW B+ (switched B+) terminal.  Fuel pump E5 should start and run."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0305",
      "reading_order": 314,
      "section": "POWER RELAY CHECK (A11-K12)",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 329.2128000000001,
        "t": 357.1291068359377,
        "r": 564.9537999999993,
        "b": 309.229449203539
      },
      "content": "Remove the B+ jumper.  If the fuel pump continues to run, K12 is good.  If the fuel pump stops, K12  has  failed  and  the  A11  control  board should be replaced."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0306",
      "reading_order": 315,
      "section": "POWER RELAY CHECK (A11-K12)",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 329.2117000000001,
        "t": 296.41130683593775,
        "r": 523.4903999999997,
        "b": 286.495749203539
      },
      "content": "Push the generator set STOP button."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0307",
      "reading_order": 316,
      "section": "POWER RELAY CHECK (A11-K12)",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 329.2117000000001,
        "t": 273.7337068359377,
        "r": 564.8239999999995,
        "b": 263.81814920353895
      },
      "content": "Remove the jumpers and reconnect CB12-2A."
    }
  ]
}